   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "Let \\( u = \\ln{\\left(x \\right)} \\) and \\( dv = \\frac{1}{x^{2}} \\, dx \\), so \\( du = \\frac{1}{x} \\, dx \\) and \\( v = - \\frac{1}{x} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Negate",
            [
               "Divide",
               1,
               "x"
            ]
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "Then the integral equals \\( \\left[- \\frac{\\ln{\\left(x \\right)}}{x}\\right]_{1}^{e} - \\int_{1}^{e} - \\frac{1}{x^{2}} \\, dx \\), and the boundary term is \\( - \\frac{1}{e} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Negate",
            [
               "Exp",
               -1
            ]
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "The remaining integral is \\( \\int_{1}^{e} - \\frac{1}{x^{2}} \\, dx = -1 + e^{-1} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Add",
            -1,
            [
               "Exp",
               -1
            ]
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 4,
         "text": "So the value is \\( - \\frac{1}{e} - \\left(-1 + e^{-1}\\right) = 1 - \\frac{2}{e} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Add",
            1,
